1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,214
Maya can't make it this afternoon.

2
00:00:03,214 --> 00:00:07,500
The coordinator reviews
the change and confirms it.

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:11,250
One cancellation has now
disrupted two commitments.

4
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:15,000
This is KindHandoff,
created by Shivam Gupta.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,065
In this fictional household,

6
00:00:17,065 --> 00:00:22,742
Maya was going to pack Arun's
library bag at two thirty,

7
00:00:22,742 --> 00:00:26,871
then drive him to book club at three.

8
00:00:26,871 --> 00:00:31,000
The ride depends on the bag being ready.

9
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:37,732
Jo can enter the house between
two and three, but cannot drive.

10
00:00:37,732 --> 00:00:43,341
Dev can drive, but is only
free from two forty-five.

11
00:00:43,341 --> 00:00:47,829
The planner checks availability,
capabilities, and conflicting commitments.

12
00:00:47,829 --> 00:00:54,000
It proposes Jo for the
bag and Dev for the ride.

13
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:58,800
A proposed plan is still only a proposal.

14
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:02,400
The coordinator creates
two handoff offers.

15
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:07,800
Jo opens her private
invitation and accepts the bag.

16
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:12,600
Dev accepts the ride in his own session.

17
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:18,000
Until each named helper accepts,
the task stays uncovered.

18
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:19,714
Watch Dev's ride.

19
00:01:19,714 --> 00:01:24,857
It is accepted, but still
waiting for the bag.

20
00:01:24,857 --> 00:01:28,286
Jo records the bag as packed.

21
00:01:28,286 --> 00:01:32,286
Only then does the ride become ready.

22
00:01:32,286 --> 00:01:35,143
Agreement and readiness stay separate,

23
00:01:35,143 --> 00:01:42,000
so an unfinished prerequisite cannot
hide behind a name on the calendar.

24
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:47,108
The handoff brief shows what
changed and what remains.

25
00:01:47,108 --> 00:01:49,946
Dev acknowledges this specific revision.

26
00:01:49,946 --> 00:01:54,486
A later update does not
rewrite that receipt.

27
00:01:54,486 --> 00:01:59,595
The circle can see who
agreed, what is ready,

28
00:01:59,595 --> 00:02:03,000
and which version each person read.

29
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:08,707
The browser's bounded language
simulator makes real MCP calls

30
00:02:08,707 --> 00:02:13,146
using the November twenty-fifth,
twenty twenty-five protocol

31
00:02:13,146 --> 00:02:15,049
and Streamable HTTP.

32
00:02:15,049 --> 00:02:18,220
Activity shows the execution trace.

33
00:02:18,220 --> 00:02:22,659
Firebase provides sign-in and
persistent household records.

34
00:02:22,659 --> 00:02:29,000
The simulator is deterministic; no
live Alexa connection is claimed.

35
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:35,061
KindHandoff starts with everyday
support: bags, rides, meals, and visits.

36
00:02:35,061 --> 00:02:41,121
The pricing hypothesis is twelve
dollars per household per month,

37
00:02:41,121 --> 00:02:43,545
with every helper included.

38
00:02:43,545 --> 00:02:45,970
Household validation comes next.

39
00:02:45,970 --> 00:02:49,000
Clear plans and accepted responsibility.
